# Force LF, including in working copies on Windows.
#
# This is not a cosmetic setting. `npm pack` archives the working copy rather than the
# committed content, so on a Windows checkout with autocrlf the published tarball would
# contain bin/afk-factory.js with CRLF line endings. On Linux the shebang then reads
# `#!/usr/bin/env node\r` and execution fails with "bad interpreter" — while everything
# keeps working for whoever published it.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
